# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in: the platform's settings and secrets. goald reads these at
# start; values never reach agent containers or logs. Taskfile.yml loads this file for every task.
# Factories' credentials are not here: they are the organization's connections (the Connections page,
# goal connection create), sealed under GOAL_MASTER_KEYS, which runs get as they need them.
# On Cloudflare the platform secrets come from Secrets Store instead (deploy/terraform/secrets/,
# docs/engineering/cloudflare-operations.md).

# Upgrading from before connections (spec 4 §14): put the old tokens here once, run
# `task connection:import-env` (it creates the connections github and claude from them), then delete
# them: goald ignores them and warns while one is set.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=               # from `claude setup-token` (one person's own use), or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GOAL_GITHUB_TOKEN=                     # a fine-grained token for the factory's repositories
# GOAL_GITHUB_WEB_URL=                   # a GitHub Enterprise's origin, when the repositories live there

# Local PostgreSQL (compose.yaml). GOAL_PG_PASSWORD is the bootstrap superuser's, used only by
# `goal db init` (goal up runs it) to create the roles: goal_owner runs migrations, goal_app runs
# goald under row-level security, goal_auth runs the identity service (apps/auth/, Better Auth's tables only).
# Give each a value of its own (openssl rand -hex 24) before the first goal up: under sign-in (the default)
# goal up refuses the dev-only defaults (goal-dev-only, goal-owner-dev-only, goal-app-dev-only,
# goal-auth-dev-only), which any process on the machine could use. goal up sets the three roles' passwords
# from here on every start; the superuser keeps the one its database was created with (ALTER ROLE goal to change it).
GOAL_PG_PASSWORD=
GOAL_PG_OWNER_PASSWORD=
GOAL_PG_APP_PASSWORD=
GOAL_PG_AUTH_PASSWORD=
# GOAL_DATABASE_ADMIN_URL=postgres://goal:goal-dev-only@127.0.0.1:5432/goal?sslmode=disable   # goal db init; default: compose's superuser

# Object storage: factory definition files (blobs under orgs/<org-id>/blobs/, versions in PostgreSQL) and the
# catalogs live in one bucket, which needs no versioning. goald reads and writes it; the CLI only for goal storage init
# and goal catalog.
# Locally RustFS (compose.yaml) stands in for S3; the access and secret keys are its dev-only root user.
# On Cloudflare: the R2 bucket goal-production at https://<account id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com, with an R2 API
# token's keys for that bucket only (terraform output bucket, s3_endpoint).
GOAL_S3_BUCKET=goal-local
GOAL_S3_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9000
GOAL_S3_ACCESS_KEY=goal-dev-only
GOAL_S3_SECRET_KEY=goal-dev-only-secret
AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# goald (cmd/goald/settings.go has every variable and its default)
# Signs the per-task MCP gateway tokens; generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`. Never reaches a task.
GOAL_GATEWAY_KEY=
# Seals connections' credentials in PostgreSQL (spec 4 §5.2): <id>:<base64 of 32 bytes>, comma-separated, the first
# active; e.g. k1:$(openssl rand -base64 32). Keep a copy offline: without it the stored credentials are lost. Unset,
# goald runs and connections with secrets are unavailable. To rotate: put a new key first, restart goald, goal db rekey,
# then drop the old one. GOAL_MASTER_KEY_FILE names a file of the same entries, one per line (mode 0600), instead.
# GOAL_MASTER_KEYS=
# A connection's test reaches public addresses only. true lets it reach this machine's and the LAN's own servers too
# (a test server on the laptop); refused unless goald listens on loopback.
# GOAL_ALLOW_PRIVATE_UPSTREAMS=false
# GOAL_MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL=postgres://goal_owner:goal-owner-dev-only@127.0.0.1:5432/goal?sslmode=disable  # migrations; default: compose's database as goal_owner
# GOAL_DATABASE_URL=postgres://goal_app:goal-app-dev-only@127.0.0.1:5432/goal?sslmode=disable  # default: compose's database as goal_app; never a superuser or owner
# GOAL_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:8080             # API, UI, and gateway without GOAL_GATEWAY_LISTEN; off loopback only with
#                                        # GOAL_AUTH=session, an https GOAL_PUBLIC_URL and GOAL_GATEWAY_LISTEN
# GOAL_GATEWAY_LISTEN=                   # the gateway's own listener, serving only /mcp (the main one then 404s /mcp);
#                                        # on Linux set the Docker bridge's address (172.17.0.1:8090) so containers reach
#                                        # the gateway and not the API; Docker Desktop and OrbStack need nothing
# GOAL_PUBLIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080  # the one origin people open goald at (https unless loopback or *.localhost;
#                                        # default http://<GOAL_LISTEN>); sign-in links and cookies follow it, and requests
#                                        # naming any other host than it, GOAL_LISTEN's and localhost/127.0.0.1/[::1] get 421.
#                                        # Running other local web servers? Use http://goal.localhost:8080: cookies are not
#                                        # port-scoped, so they would get the session cookie (SECURITY.md)
# GOAL_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080     # where the goal CLI finds goald
# GOAL_GATEWAY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/mcp  # the gateway's URL; default follows GOAL_GATEWAY_LISTEN. Agent containers get the egress proxy's address at its path
# Agent containers run on compose.yaml's agents network and reach public hosts, and goald's /mcp and /run, only through its goal-egress
# service; never the host, a private or a metadata address (ADR 0009 and its phase 4 amendment; goal up starts it, task egress:image builds it):
# GOAL_SANDBOX_NETWORK=goal_agents        # the agents network's name, for compose and goald alike
# GOAL_EGRESS_GATEWAY=                    # goald's gateway listener as goal-egress reaches it; goal up derives it from GOAL_GATEWAY_URL or the
#                                         # listener (http://host.docker.internal:8080 by default; http://goald:8090 under goal up --compose)
# GOAL_DOCKER_GID=0                       # goal up --compose on Linux: the Docker socket's group (stat -c %g /var/run/docker.sock)
# GOAL_AGENT_IMAGE=ghcr.io/byfrederick/goal-agent:0.2.0  # every run's sandbox (task up builds it from the checkout); runtime.image is ignored
# GOAL_SANDBOX=docker                     # where runs' sandboxes run: docker, or cloudflare (the control Worker sets it, with
#                                         # GOAL_SANDBOX_URL=http://sandbox.internal and GOAL_SANDBOX_KEY, deploy/cloudflare)
# GOAL_AGENT_EGRESS, GOAL_EGRESS_NAME, GOAL_EGRESS_IMAGE, GOAL_WORKSPACE_ROOT, GOAL_RUN_DIR, GOAL_DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE,
# GOAL_TASK_ENV, GOAL_GITHUB_API_URL and GOAL_GITHUB_WEB_URL are gone: goald warns while one is set, naming what
#                                         # replaced it, and ignores it (a run's model is its factory's runtime.modelConnection)
# The knowledge base (spec 4 §4.8): keyword search only until GOAL_EMBED_URL names an OpenAI-compatible embeddings API,
# then hybrid search. The provider sees the indexed text; a local model (Ollama) keeps it on this machine.
# GOAL_EMBED_URL=                         # e.g. https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/<account id>/ai/v1 (Workers AI)
#                                         # or http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1 (Ollama, with GOAL_ALLOW_PRIVATE_UPSTREAMS=true: goald's
#                                         # requests reach public addresses only); https unless loopback or a local name
# GOAL_EMBED_MODEL=@cf/baai/bge-m3        # a model of 1024 dimensions (Ollama: bge-m3); changing it re-embeds every source
# GOAL_EMBED_KEY=                         # its bearer key (Workers AI: an API token with Workers AI Read)
# GOAL_KB_WORKERS=2                       # sources this goald syncs at once (0: none)
# GOAL_UPLOAD_MAX_BYTES=26214400          # the largest file uploaded to the knowledge base (25 MiB)
# GOAL_TICK_EVERY=5s  GOAL_REFRESH_EVERY=30s  GOAL_LOG_LEVEL=info  GOAL_LOG_FORMAT=json
# GOAL_DEFINITION_CACHE_BYTES=67108864   # files of versions no longer current kept for the runs pinned to them
# GOAL_MAX_RUNS=0                        # agent runs one goald runs at once, shared fairly across organizations; 0 = no cap
# GOAL_MODELS=claude-opus-5-5,claude-sonnet-5-5,claude-haiku-5-5  # models the factory editor offers, the first is the default (id or id=Label)

# Sign-in (spec 3). Under GOAL_AUTH=session goal up starts the identity service
# (node apps/auth/dist/server.js, `task auth:build`) and Mailpit beside goald, and gives each process only
# its own variables: goald never sees the auth service's secrets below.
# GOAL_AUTH=session                      # the default; none: no sign-in, every request is the single local user (loopback only,
#                                        # one developer's laptop; turn it back on any time without losing data)
# The auth service's secret: session signing and token encryption; `openssl rand -hex 32`, never GOAL_GATEWAY_KEY.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRETS=                   # instead, to rotate: versioned secrets, newest first (2:<new>,1:<old>)
# GOAL_AUTH_PROXY_SECRET=                # goald sends it with every request to the auth service, which refuses any other;
#                                        # goal up generates one per start; set one (openssl rand -hex 32) to run goald
#                                        # and the auth service yourself (task goald, task auth:dev)
# The first owner's address: while nobody has signed in it is the only one that may, and becomes platform
# admin and owner of every organization. A mistake is fixed here and with a restart, until that first sign-in.
GOAL_BOOTSTRAP_OWNER_EMAIL=        # such as owner@example.com
# GOAL_SMTP_URL=smtp://127.0.0.1:1025    # where codes and invitations are mailed (smtps:// with user:password for a
#                                        # real server); default compose's Mailpit, read at http://127.0.0.1:8025 as user
#                                        # goal with the password goal up generates into ~/.config/goal/mailpit-ui-auth
# GOAL_SMTP_FROM=Goal <goal@localhost>   # the sender
# GOAL_SMTP_PLAINTEXT=off                # smtp:// off loopback must offer STARTTLS; on: send unencrypted, allowed only to
#                                        # compose's Mailpit, smtp://mailpit:1025 (goal up --compose sets it in compose.yaml)
# GOAL_AUTH_GOOGLE=off                   # on: also sign in with Google (an OAuth client of type Web application whose
#                                        # redirect URI is <GOAL_PUBLIC_URL>/api/auth/callback/google)
# GOAL_AUTH_EMAIL=on                     # off: no email codes and no mail at all, for an install without a mail server;
#                                        # needs GOAL_AUTH_GOOGLE=on (goald and the auth service both read it)
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOAL_AUTH_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:8081        # the identity service's address, loopback only (goald's /api/auth proxy is the way in)
# GOAL_AUTH_UPSTREAM=http://127.0.0.1:8081  # where goald's proxy reaches it (http on loopback; on Cloudflare http://auth.internal)
# GOAL_AUTH_DATABASE_URL=postgres://goal_auth:goal-auth-dev-only@127.0.0.1:5432/goal?sslmode=disable  # default from GOAL_PG_AUTH_PASSWORD
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=                       # leave unset: it must equal GOAL_PUBLIC_URL
# GOAL_TRUSTED_PROXIES=                  # CIDRs of proxies in front of goald whose X-Forwarded-For names the client
#                                        # (none on a laptop or compose; the control Worker sets it on Cloudflare)
# The CLI: goal login keeps its session in the OS keychain; for scripts and CI an API key (goal_sk_…) or a
# personal token (goal_pat_…) from the UI instead, which acts in its own organization.
# GOAL_API_KEY=
# GOAL_ORG=                              # the organization CLI commands act in (else goal org use's)

# goal catalog skills sync (operator): skills from skills.sh, read from GitHub
# GOAL_SKILLS_DIRECTORY_URL=https://skills.sh
GOAL_SKILLS_DIRECTORY_TOKEN=  # bearer token of the skills.sh API; only --search needs it
# GOAL_SKILLS_GITHUB_TOKEN=     # optional: raises GitHub's rate limit (public repositories need none)
# GOAL_SKILLS_GITHUB_API_URL=https://api.github.com

# Local working copy of the factory definitions (outside this repository, not under git)
GOAL_FACTORIES_DIR=../goal-factories
